{
 "header": {
  "probe": "P3",
  "question": "P3: does a .mcc file holding one key leave every other setting alone? Commander is closed (WM_CLOSE) and started again with no file, the control, since a plain restart can itself bring back some I-Clamp values changed [verified 2026-10-23, Q23, Q12]; then with a file holding only the V-Clamp feedback resistor, ELCTRD_HSTAGE_RST_RNG=1 (500 M\u03a9) in [MC700_CHANNEL1_VCLAMP]; then with one holding only the start's index (5 G\u03a9 as found), and, if a feedback resistor still differs from the start, with one holding both tabs' start indexes. After each, what the API reaches is put back to the start, so each starts from the same state. Before and after each, both tabs are read in V-Clamp, I = 0, I-Clamp and V-Clamp again, both output signals set again in each mode first (the telegraph's are stale after a start), and each page of Commander's Options dialog is screenshot (filter type, Sync Output, External Command Sensitivity, the Auto, Audio and Advanced pages: what no API reads). The answer is each step's `besides_feedback_resistor`: what differs from before other than the V-Clamp feedback resistor and the telegraph's V-Clamp scale factors, which follow it. The files are written to --log-dir, which must hold no space.",
  "time": "2026-10-23T17:16:04.147110-04:00",
  "setup": "amplifier on, a model cell on the headstage, its switch at CELL (--model-cell CELL)",
  "commander": "2.2.2.2",
